<title>INDONESIA: TABLE-BAT Indonesia first half net up.</title>
<headline>TABLE-BAT Indonesia first half net up.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>	    (in billion rupiah except per share)</p>
<p>    Net profit			    20.87    vs   20.69</p>
<p>    Earnings per share (rupiah)	 948    vs    940</p>
<p>    Net sales			     169.42   vs   137.32</p>
<p>    Operating profit		     39.20   vs    30.41</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			 30.14   vs    28.78</p>
<p>    Retained earnings		    40.17   vs    29.40</p>
<p>NOTE: PT BAT Indonesia, a subsidiary of British tobacco giant B.A.T. Industries is a cigarette firm.</p>
